 62, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -5.78, "lead_after": -6.0, "points_lost": -0.22, "best": "C9"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Trading Blunders Down to a Six-Point Margin", "summary": "The 20k, playing White, won by 6 after both passed. The game was nearly even for the first ten moves, then GPT-6.1 Sol lost 6.5 points at move 11 and kept losing big chunks (8 blunders, 5.0 points per move on average). The 20k blundered nearly as often (6 blunders, 4.8 per move) and handed several of those points back, so it ended at W+6 rather than a rout.", "moments": [{"turn": 11, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's C4 is where the even game slipped: the lead went from -1.8 to -8.2, a 6.5-point loss, and the engine wanted F3. White's F3 later became the key point of the bottom."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "After White's E4 let the lead swing from -8.5 to +2.2, GPT-6.1 Sol had a real chance to get back into the game. G6 gave it straight back: 11.4 points lost, +2.2 to -9.2, where the engine preferred H3."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "E2 fell into the shadow of White's long wall along row 4 and cost 21.0 points, taking the lead from -10.3 to -31.2. The engine's choice was E8, up at the top, away from the cramped bottom."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "A3 was GPT-6.1 Sol's worst move of the game, 24.1 points, dropping the lead from -8.2 to -32.3. It came right after the 20k's A4 had itself lost 26.2 points. Both sides were swinging wildly in the lower-left corner, and the engine's choice was H8."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "H7 had just lost 20.3 points, and the 20k's G8 answered it with the game's biggest single loss, 27.3 points. The lead went from -33.4 back to -6.1, and the game then settled into passes at about W+6."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either called the go tools (choose_opponent, play, board), read or wrote record files, or ran the inspection and verification code (inspect85, verify85), which only parse a supplied board into groups, liberties, regions and area and replay the already-played moves to check legality and captures. None of it generated, scored or ranked candidate moves or looked ahead, and every move was passed to play as a hand-picked literal.", "stop": false}}